# fs adjacent-call notes

The opening of build_themes.js puts the file and path objects together. Line 7 binds fs, and line 8 binds path; root on line 10 takes __dirname directly. The directory value is not passed in through another configuration object; the theme build script resolves locations from its own directory.

```js
const fs = require("fs");
const path = require("path");
const root = __dirname;
const themesDir = path.join(root, "app/assets/stylesheets/themes");
```

themesDir on line 11 is the themes styles directory. Line 12 then declares buildsDir, so the two directory values should be read together with root, rather than treating themesDir as a temporary path generated only inside themeSlugs.

themeSlugs is on line 14, and copyBootstrapIconFonts is on line 22. The former's name corresponds to theme identification, and the latter's to copying Bootstrap icon fonts; these notes do not cover the call order between the two functions. When reading the code adjacent to fs calls, first confirm where the directory constants come from, then examine the file operations handled by each of these two functions.
